---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
---

<Base
  title="about — monesh"
  description="About Monesh B. — infrastructure and tooling engineer."
>
  <Breadcrumb />
  <h1 class="page-h1 essay-h1">About</h1>
  <p class="page-subline">about.md &middot; serif</p>
  <article class="prose-essay">
    <p>
      I&rsquo;m Monesh &mdash; an infrastructure and tooling engineer who builds
      developer platforms with agentic workflows. The work under this directory
      is the portfolio: projects with full write-ups, essays on the engineering
      choices that got me to them.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      I lean on agentic tools for the parts of engineering work that are
      mechanical at scale &mdash; dependency-graph extraction, code-mod scripts,
      exhaustive surface scans, anything tedious enough that I&rsquo;d lose track
      doing it by hand. The judgment calls stay mine. Trust the agent&rsquo;s
      outputs, verify them against the ground truth, codify the verification.
      See <a href="/writing/decoupling-the-monorepo">decoupling-the-monorepo</a>
      for a worked example.
    </p>

    <h2>Where I&rsquo;m useful</h2>
    <p>
      Small teams that need infrastructure work done correctly the first time.
      Dev tooling that disappears once it works. Bounded-scope ownership of a
      load-bearing surface &mdash; build systems, deploy pipelines, internal
      CLIs, the kind of code that runs every day and that nobody wants to debug
      at 3am.
    </p>
    <p>
      I&rsquo;m currently in Hyderabad and open to remote roles or on-site work
      that includes a relocation discussion.
    </p>

    <h2>How to reach me</h2>
    <p>
      Email is on <a href="/contact">/contact</a>. I respond within 24 hours
      during the week.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
